# Agent Knowledge Index

Use these documents for durable project knowledge. Keep `AGENTS.md` short and link here instead of expanding always-loaded instructions.

Knowledge metadata is tracked in `.agent/knowledge.json`. Update `owner`, `last_reviewed`, `source_links`, and `known_stale_sections` when durable knowledge changes.
Cross-session working memory is tracked in `.agent/memory.json` and `.agent/memory/`. Store summaries, decisions, validation, and retrieval handles; do not store raw transcripts.
Embedded specification management is tracked in `.agent/spec.json` and `openspec/`; use `scripts/agent_spec.py` for change lifecycle commands.
Capability governance is tracked in `.agent/capabilities.json`. Run evidence is tracked in `.agent/runlog.jsonl`.
Agent-facing inspection limits are tracked in `.agent/tooling.json`. Security and supply-chain suites are tracked in `.agent/security.json`.
Workflow gates, including risk classification, implementation discipline, diff traceability, and review evidence, are tracked in `.agent/workflow.json`.
Risk autonomy is tracked in `.agent/risk-zones.json`. Diff and review policy is tracked in `.agent/review-policy.json`.
Isolated worktree policy is tracked in `.agent/worktrees.json`.
Governance health scoring is tracked in `.agent/evals.json` and `.agent/evals/latest.md`.

- [Architecture](ARCHITECTURE.md): system boundaries, dependency direction, and major design decisions.
- [Quality](QUALITY.md): build, test, lint, typecheck, and review expectations.
- [Reliability](RELIABILITY.md): runtime behavior, observability, rollback, and operational risks.
- [Security](SECURITY.md): secrets, auth, sensitive data, and dependency risk rules.
- [Agent Tooling](TOOLING.md): bounded repository inspection, search, and output rules.
- [Governance Score](QUALITY_SCORE.md): local score dimensions, dashboard, and drift signals.
- [AI Coding Glossary](AI_CODING_GLOSSARY.md): shared terms for skills, tools, MCP, harness, sessions, memory, and reviews.
- [Tech Debt](tech-debt.md): known debt, cleanup candidates, and follow-up work.
- [ADRs](adr/README.md): durable architecture decisions.
- [RFCs](rfcs/README.md): pre-change design proposals.
- [Incidents](incidents/README.md): postmortems and reliability learning.

Update `.agent/harness.json` when validation commands or required docs change.
Update `.agent/spec.json` when embedded spec paths, artifacts, or lifecycle policy change.
Update `.agent/workflow.json` when lifecycle gates, risk classification, implementation discipline, diff traceability, review order, TDD/debugging rules, or completion evidence rules change.
Update `.agent/risk-zones.json` when risk levels, autonomy rules, approval gates, or high-risk path patterns change.
Update `.agent/review-policy.json` when diff traceability categories, human review evidence, or automated review boundaries change.
Update `.agent/worktrees.json` when isolated worktree locations, baseline validation, or guarded cleanup rules change.
Update `.agent/subagents.json` when delegated agent roles, boundaries, or snapshot rules change.
Update `.agent/hooks.json` when session bootstrap, checkpoint, or native hook adapter behavior changes.
Update `.agent/memory.json` when memory stores, privacy tags, or retention policy change.
Update `.agent/capabilities.json` when agent-visible tools, external integrations, permissions, owners, or risk levels change.
Update `.agent/runlog.jsonl` through `scripts/agent_runlog.py` or generated validation/session tools; do not edit raw evidence unless repairing invalid JSONL.
Update `.agent/tooling.json` when output limits, ignored directories, or bounded inspection rules change.
Update `.agent/security.json` when policy-as-code, secret scan, dependency audit, SBOM, or license scan commands change.
Update `.agent/evals.json` when score dimensions, thresholds, cadence, or dashboard stores change.
Update `.agent/skill-distribution.json` when project skill synchronization paths change.
